flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1["Complete the following checks: 1. Inspect the belt<br/>surface for cuts, gouges, or embedded debris. 2.<br/>Check the splice joint for separation or edge<br/>lifting. 3. Inspect both pulley faces for grooving<br/>or material buildup."]
    box_2{"Belt damage assessment, splice failure or deep cuts?"}
    box_3(["End, Escalate: belt replacement required, production<br/>hold"])
    box_4["Run the conveyor belt at normal operating speed with<br/>no product load. Observe belt tracking from the<br/>drive end across the full belt width. Record whether<br/>the belt drifts toward the drive side, the idler<br/>side, or remains centred. Mark any sections where<br/>the belt edge contacts the frame or guide flange."]
    box_5[/"Refer to the belt tracking specification."/]
    box_6{"Belt tracking within ±5 mm of centreline?"}
    box_7["Adjust tracking via tail roller tilt, half turn<br/>increments"]
    box_8{"Reverify belt tracking after tail roller adjustment"}
    box_9(["End, Escalate: chronic tracking fault, frame<br/>alignment check required"])
    box_10["Stop the belt and locate the measurement point at<br/>the centre span between the two middle idler<br/>rollers. Apply a calibrated force perpendicular to<br/>the belt surface equal to the value in the belt<br/>specification and measure the resulting deflection<br/>with a steel rule. Compare the measured deflection<br/>against the allowable range and record both figures<br/>in the maintenance log."]
    box_11[/"Refer to the belt tension specification."/]
    box_12{"Belt tension within specified deflection range?"}
    box_13["Adjust take up tensioner to correct belt deflection"]
    box_14{"Reverify belt tension after take up adjustment"}
    box_15(["End, Escalate: take up travel exhausted, belt<br/>stretch limit reached"])
    box_16["Spin each roller by hand and listen for roughness,<br/>rumbling, or intermittent drag indicating bearing<br/>wear. Using a dial test indicator on a magnetic<br/>base, measure radial runout at the roller face at<br/>three positions along the length. Note any rollers<br/>that show surface damage, flat spots, or material<br/>build up that could cause belt scrubbing."]
    box_17{"All idler rollers rotate freely with no flat spots?"}
    box_18["Replace seized or worn idler rollers"]
    box_19["With the motor running at operating speed under<br/>normal belt load, hold an infrared thermometer<br/>approximately 50 millimetres from the drive motor<br/>end cap and record the surface temperature. Wait<br/>five minutes and repeat at the opposite end cap.<br/>Compare both readings against the maximum rated<br/>housing temperature on the motor nameplate."]
    box_20{"Drive motor temperature within rated limit?"}
    box_21(["End, Escalate: motor overtemperature, check cooling<br/>and load"])
    box_22["Stop the drive and hang a plumb line from a fixed<br/>pin through two corresponding link plates, then<br/>measure vertical sag at the mid span. Calculate<br/>percentage elongation against the nominal pitch<br/>length from the chain specification. Inspect the<br/>side plates for cracks and the roller surfaces for<br/>pitting, then verify that the chain is coated in the<br/>correct lubricant grade."]
    box_23[/"Refer to the drive chain wear limit."/]
    box_24{"Drive chain elongation within wear limit?"}
    box_25["Replace drive chain and retension to specification"]
    box_26["Jog the conveyor slowly until a reference part<br/>reaches the end of line sensor and observe the<br/>sensor indicator light. Measure the distance from<br/>the part leading edge to the sensor face at the<br/>trigger point using a steel rule. Compare against<br/>the setpoint distance specified on the sensor setup<br/>drawing and adjust the bracket position if the<br/>trigger point is outside tolerance."]
    box_27{"End of line sensor trigger point within ±2 mm<br/>tolerance?"}
    box_28["Reposition sensor bracket and reteach trigger point"]
    box_29["Load test, run 50 parts through conveyor at<br/>production speed"]
    box_30{"Load test passed, no tracking deviation or jams?"}
    box_31["Log all measurements and update conveyor service<br/>record"]
    box_32(["End, Procedure complete"])
    box_33["Secondary belt tracking correction: slacken the tail<br/>roller locking bolts and adjust the roller end that<br/>is opposite to the direction of belt drift in 2<br/>millimetre increments. Run the belt for two minutes<br/>between each adjustment to allow the tracking<br/>response to stabilise. Check frame squareness with a<br/>precision square before returning to the belt<br/>tracking observation step."]

